WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:09.480
Is there any good news in the polls for
Donald Trump at the six-month mark of

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:14.670
his presidency? The simple answer is: not
much. He is less popular than any other

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:18.750
president of this point in his tenure in
terms of his overall approval rating.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:22.859
President Obama's approval rating in the
summer his first year in office was

00:00:22.859 --> 00:00:27.869
around 60 percent. Trump's approval rating
hovers around 40 percent. President Trump gets

00:00:27.869 --> 00:00:31.710
negative marks on handling foreign
policy and health care. People are split

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:35.850
about his handling of the economy. The
president still has the support of most

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.530
Republicans; slightly more than 80% of
them approve of the job that he's doing.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:45.420
But large majorities of independents and
Democrats disapproved. Democrats

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:50.219
especially disapprove intensely. But
there is one bright spot in an otherwise

00:00:50.219 --> 00:00:54.510
dismal poll landscape for the
president: Although Americans give Barack

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:58.710
Obama more credit than Trump for the
economy's resilience, President Trump

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:03.719
gets generally positive marks on job
creation and keeping jobs at home, both

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:06.620
of which are high priorities for most
Americans. How do you think President

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:11.260
How do you think President Trump is doing? Let us know in your comments.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:15.660
Also, let us know what other topics you'd like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:21.020
and be sure to subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

